{"connection_id": "BC-16112518248feb939a3e", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.11", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Open and sealed copies", "note": "The purchase deed exists in both sealed and open forms, a specific legal record parallel to the commentary's account of writing and witnesses."}
{"connection_id": "BC-07a1a1d6c845444dffc5", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.12", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Witnesses see the deed", "note": "The deed is handed to Baruch in the presence of witnesses, echoing the commentary's emphasis on a witness in a recorded obligation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2a9c75633c82de7b24d8", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.14", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Preserve the record for later proof", "note": "The deeds are stored so they may last many days, giving a concrete scriptural purpose for accurate records beyond the immediate transaction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e41c8f9118d42cc25928", "ref": "WLC:Jer.50.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost sheep led astray by their shepherds", "note": "Jeremiah's people are lost sheep whose leaders turned them from their resting place, directly meeting wrong guidance, herd, and home."}
{"connection_id": "BC-80dec324ebef61dba179", "ref": "WLC:Jer.7.23", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "obey, be my people, walk the commanded way", "note": "Jeremiah makes obedience and walking the commanded way the condition of belonging to God, clarifying the commentary's owned servant who addresses the true master."}
{"connection_id": "BC-038978a101cef5204e78", "ref": "WLC:Jer.8.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sun, moon, and stars loved, served, followed, and worshipped", "note": "Jeremiah explicitly combines astral worship with service and following, a very close counterpart to the commentary's celestial false lords and path imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6ce941ac656aa5f729a0", "ref": "WLC:Job.31.26", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sun shining and moon moving in splendor", "note": "Job names the very visual appeal of sun and moon that makes the commentary's ascending celestial signs a test of discernment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ad63e67b479e04a5a3b", "ref": "WLC:Job.31.27", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "heart secretly enticed; hand kissed in worship", "note": "The next verse identifies the move from seeing luminaries to idolatrous devotion, making explicit the error the commentary assigns to sun-worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-65fcb87d01916f12f833", "ref": "WLC:Job.31.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "let God weigh me in just balances", "note": "Job asks for divine weighing that will disclose integrity, directly pairing balance with the final moral account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4420b723ad5d5ad12de7", "ref": "WLC:Joel.3.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The dreadful day of YHWH", "note": "The sun and moon darken before the great day of YHWH, a concrete “day of God” judgment image for the commentary's days of punishment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1fdc3f686056ddef9c2d", "ref": "WLC:Joel.3.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Rescue for those who call on YHWH", "note": "The same oracle promises deliverance to those who call on YHWH, giving the day both judgment and rescue as in the commentary's paired punishment and forgiveness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d9700e606ec5803a0271", "ref": "WLC:Josh.22.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "na'budu; Hebrew la'avod; walk all his ways", "note": "Joshua joins serving YHWH with walking all his ways; Hebrew avad is cognate with the commentary's na'budu, making its service-and-road equation concrete."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b6081bf4926f29f09dd5", "ref": "WLC:Lev.1.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "offering drawn from cattle or flock", "note": "Leviticus supplies the sacrificial category of herd and flock behind the commentary's animal separated for an offering, without its full homeward scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-66856b6ef21158b906dd", "ref": "WLC:Lev.19.36", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "just balances and just weights", "note": "The Torah's command makes an unbent balance an ethical demand, supplying the legal ground for the commentary's warning about deficient measure."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b397782de1895c089e7a", "ref": "WLC:Lev.25.55", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Israelites are my servants, brought from Egypt", "note": "Leviticus opposes Egyptian bondage to belonging as God's servants; Hebrew avadim is cognate with Arabic abd and makes the true-owner contrast explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4140ca8eee115255f66a", "ref": "WLC:Mal.3.18", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "distinguish one who serves God from one who does not", "note": "Malachi makes service to God the criterion separating two destinies as judgment approaches, closely matching the commentary's willing servant and two outcomes."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ed981e22d234a5449489", "ref": "WLC:Mic.2.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the breaker and king go before the people", "note": "Micah imagines a path opened and a king going at the people's head, a strong counterpart to the commentary's guide who precedes the community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6baf40f2a9d7a908f3e3", "ref": "WLC:Mic.7.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "though fallen, I rise; darkness becomes light", "note": "Micah gives the commentary's fallen and upright walker an explicit scriptural reversal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8072a04b457f5348e5f9", "ref": "WLC:Neh.5.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "children enslaved because of debt", "note": "Nehemiah joins debt to forced enslavement in a concrete social scene, illuminating the commentary's juxtaposition of debt and coerced servitude."}
{"connection_id": "BC-690cf10f56ebaf7964a0", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "host of heaven worships its maker", "note": "Nehemiah reverses astral worship: the heavenly host itself worships YHWH, so celestial things become servants rather than lords."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5cb28ff847ddd99f320a", "ref": "WLC:Num.27.17", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "leader goes out before the people so they are not sheep without a shepherd", "note": "Moses asks for a leader who goes before and leads the congregation, explicitly joining the traveller-guide and herd-leader images."}
{"connection_id": "BC-181ca27859c4ffa23bf4", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.27", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ism; Hebrew šēm", "note": "The commentary reads the surah's opening name as an identifying sign; this verse says God's name is placed upon Israel in blessing, a concrete use of the cognate name-word as belonging and blessing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3fb54916b1f6d98e9710", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.27", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's name rests on the people as blessing", "note": "The priests place YHWH's name upon Israel and bless them, giving the commentary's opening name-as-identifying-sign a liturgical and communal form."}
{"connection_id": "BC-438a77f2e5a715152e1b", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.27", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "put my name on Israel and bless them", "note": "The priestly formula treats the divine name as a mark of belonging and blessing, illuminating name, sign, and completed favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-90fb194fd56692c96756", "ref": "WLC:Num.9.17", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The cloud's movement sets the community on the road", "note": "Israel travels when the cloud lifts and camps when it settles, giving the community a guide who determines the path and its timing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7d874c82112b4f1b405f", "ref": "WLC:Num.9.18", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Israel travels at YHWH's command", "note": "The people move and remain according to YHWH's word, a specific expression of collective dependence on guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-331048f1447bec9057e5", "ref": "WLC:Prov.11.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Honest weights please YHWH", "note": "The proverb says false scales are detestable to YHWH but accurate weights please him, directly joining the commentary's balance image to divine judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cbb7fed74133628d01ab", "ref": "WLC:Prov.11.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "false balance and just weight", "note": "The proverb sets deceitful scale against the weight God delights in, sharpening the commentary's moral reading of the mizan."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d486955ae9a27380a8ee", "ref": "WLC:Prov.4.18", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The righteous path grows brighter", "note": "The just person's path is dawn light growing brighter, closely matching the commentary's upright walking on a straight path."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e2280c0356867f467e13", "ref": "WLC:Prov.4.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The wicked stumble in darkness", "note": "The wicked walk in darkness and do not know what makes them stumble, a precise parallel to the commentary's lost traveler and fallen person under wrath."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f6ce95fb668de0351169", "ref": "WLC:Prov.4.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "way of wicked is darkness; they do not know what makes them stumble", "note": "Proverbs makes lost direction visible as a walker who stumbles without knowing why, closely matching the commentary's fallen wayfarer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-836cf26f3edb1aeb7c70", "ref": "WLC:Prov.4.26", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "level path of your feet", "note": "Proverbs tells the walker to level the track under his feet, directly supplying the commentary's image of feet making a road surface straight and firm."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b882c36886adc6772f3e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The blessed person meditates on Torah day and night", "note": "The psalm defines the blessed person's way through delight in God's instruction, adding a Torah-centered Jewish account of how the favored path is walked."}
{"connection_id": "BC-08294f11ef8f2d7edd51", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The righteous are planted beside water", "note": "The person on the good way is like a tree planted beside streams, bearing fruit in season; this links the blessed path to the commentary's water and nourishment imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d58cf09d5ba1fe43460d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic qāma; Hebrew q-w-m", "note": "The commentary joins a standing balance to people standing on judgment day; the Hebrew cognate q-w-m says the wicked will not stand in the judgment assembly."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1f7848a4fdcaa42e2a17", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "wicked will not stand in the judgment", "note": "Hebrew qum, to stand, is cognate with the commentary's qama, and the verse places that standing exactly in the judgment scene."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-2b51a81b47e6119ee2fe", "ref": "WLC:Ps.100.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Creator, owner, and flock", "note": "The psalm says YHWH made the people and that they are his people and flock; this closely meets the commentary's move from Lordship to owned worshippers and a guided herd."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e937f4b7fdd80601bd1", "ref": "WLC:Ps.100.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Thanksgiving at the gates", "note": "The worshippers enter God's gates with thanksgiving and praise, a liturgical path toward the divine house that complements the commentary's praise and destination-house imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-58a0ab47119862e132fb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Praise blesses God's name", "note": "The psalmist commands his soul to bless YHWH's holy name, matching the commentary's opening movement from the named Lord to praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7b81b393dce5d699b1d2", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "father's compassion for children", "note": "Psalm 103 uses the r-h-m root for a father's compassion toward children, adding a paternal form to the commentary's nurturing Rabb and rahim."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ce005695fab00bc16c56", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The Lord's throne over all", "note": "YHWH establishes his throne in heaven and rules over all, directly complementing the commentary's Lord of all worlds and master of the judgment day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-198337f7f3b601f12339", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Praise before benefits are recounted", "note": "The speaker says not to forget God's benefits immediately after praising him, echoing the commentary's observation that praise comes before the gifts are named."}
{"connection_id": "BC-92697c8f1c555dd5cb39", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.20", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Heavenly servants bless the Lord", "note": "The psalm calls powerful heavenly servants to obey God's word and bless him, extending praise beyond the human petitioner to the created order."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c63e09e83562da1d61d5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.22", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "All creation praises its ruler", "note": "The closing call to all God's works to bless him matches the commentary's universal Lordship and praise before any specific benefit is named."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8cbc15594b95129b48c5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Forgiveness and healing", "note": "The benefits named are forgiveness and healing, giving content to the commentary's claim that divine mercy completes the good received from the Lord."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7ec3da158399ced00662", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Love crowns the recipient", "note": "God crowns the worshipper with steadfast love and compassion, connecting the commentary's blessing-completed-by-mercy image to a concrete praise text."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d2f9d2a4c7c499ba1f89", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Renewed strength and provision", "note": "The psalm says God satisfies the worshipper with good and renews life, a specific image of divine nurture after praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7cd02b5bce096cfe3f69", "ref": "WLC:Ps.103.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Compassionate and gracious Lord", "note": "This reprise of YHWH's merciful attributes closely matches the Fatiha's mercy names and the commentary's emphasis on God's completed care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ccffb3b6208c20c4f321", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "springs sent into valleys to run among mountains", "note": "The creator directs springs through the land, a strong biblical image for water set into a traversable landscape."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fcc5c538f04541b5ceb6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.11", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wild animals drink from the springs", "note": "The springs meet the thirst of animals, directly extending the commentary's convergence of water and herd."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d59ab8f48634392de105", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.14", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "grass for livestock and food from the earth", "note": "God's vegetation feeds both livestock and humans, closely matching the commentary's Rabb who nourishes creatures through plant growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cea9fcb95b342671bd2c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Wanderers cannot find a way to an inhabited city", "note": "The psalm describes hungry and thirsty travelers lost in a wilderness with no city in reach, closely meeting the commentary's lost traveler and destination-home imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4ae880e45cc5de922c47", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wandered without a way to an inhabited city", "note": "The psalm begins with people lost on a desert route and unable to find a city to dwell in, closely matching the commentary's road without its final home."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ac5694d62b5a7750a9ce", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hungry, thirsty, and fainting on the way", "note": "The travellers' thirst and failing strength give a direct biblical counterpart to the weary wayfarer who asks the Rabb for help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c25df28335a161b30f33", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The lost cry to YHWH for help", "note": "The wanderers cry to God in distress and he rescues them, matching the commentary's needy traveler who asks the Lord for aid."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bb2bf7defa5eba75ec52", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads them by a straight way to a city", "note": "YHWH guides the travelers on a straight road to an inhabited city, joining the commentary's requested guidance, straight path, and arrival place in one scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2bd46466e0145879fa85", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "led by a straight way to a city to dwell in", "note": "YHWH leads the lost travellers on a straight way to habitation, combining guidance, road, and house in the commentary's exact sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-12d1e256ac65f7e9bdbd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Thanks for steadfast love after rescue", "note": "The rescued are urged to thank YHWH for his steadfast love, linking praise to the help received along the road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a9096574d364a6ab2104", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God satisfies the thirsty and hungry", "note": "God fills the hungry and satisfies the thirsty, adding provision to the lost traveler's rescue and the commentary's water imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1d788dfe08055929f883", "ref": "WLC:Ps.116.17", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Thanksgiving offering and invocation of the name", "note": "The speaker offers a sacrifice of thanksgiving and calls on YHWH's name, matching the commentary's named offering and worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6d661bbf6c0c04fc8c8a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.116.18", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The vow is paid before the people", "note": "The speaker fulfills vows in the presence of God's people, giving a public setting to the act of offering and praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fefa73f87bca7add99cd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.116.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The offering reaches the Lord's house", "note": "The vow is fulfilled in Jerusalem, in the courts of YHWH's house, directly joining sacrifice, name, worship, and the destination house."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b5204612581fcecb6268", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.105", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lamp for my feet and light for my path", "note": "The word gives a walker light exactly at the feet and on the path, sharpening the commentary's concrete imagery of movement and guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-729a23b5a3667e6aac0d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.176", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost sheep; seek your servant", "note": "The speaker is simultaneously a strayed sheep and God's servant who asks to be sought, tightly joining dallin, herd, and worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9deb13af632844ec7357", "ref": "WLC:Ps.121.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A traveler's question about help", "note": "The pilgrim looks to the hills and asks where help will come from, closely echoing the Fatiha's tired traveler's request for help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c957c291594345bff34c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.121.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Help from the creator", "note": "The answer locates help in YHWH, maker of heaven and earth, joining the commentary's help petition to its praise of the Lord of all realms."}
{"connection_id": "BC-274a542eda9d2b5bf5e7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.121.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "YHWH is shade at your right hand", "note": "The divine keeper as shade on the traveller's side gives a compact biblical counterpart to the commentary's shade and sustaining help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e5a24fac61f2dd44bacc", "ref": "WLC:Ps.139.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hand leads and right hand holds", "note": "The psalm makes being led and physically held together, illuminating the commentary's traveller supported while he walks."}
{"connection_id": "BC-372368a2620c6994cbcf", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's good spirit leads on level ground", "note": "The psalm asks God's spirit to lead the speaker on level ground, a direct image of the upright path and guide developed in the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-02c5c7e8cdb6a67f6e2a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teach me to do your will; lead me on level ground", "note": "Prayer for obedience and for the good Spirit to lead on level ground links voluntary service, help, and an upright route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-00faad129940ac1e7377", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Show me the way I should walk", "note": "The speaker asks God to let him hear steadfast love and show the way to go, closely joining the Fatiha's request for guidance with its reliance on mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-78c119d0d66c75889069", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's kingdom is everlasting and faithful", "note": "The psalm's account of God's enduring kingdom joins praise of divine sovereignty to the commentary's master of the judgment day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0d9aafd1ad3360c3e1a5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.15", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "All creatures look to God for food", "note": "Every living thing looks to God for sustenance, matching the commentary's picture of the needy traveler and its Lord who provides."}
