{"connection_id": "BC-9ec7f456744f150ac68b", "ref": "Mishnah Avot 3:16", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "credit, open ledger, writing hand, collectors, true judgment", "note": "Avot's shop-and-ledger parable unites debt, recorded accounts, payment, and a true judgment in the exact cluster developed in the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a2ce1cdfcfb8d55cb269", "ref": "Mishnah Avot 4:22", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "formed, born, die, and give account before the King of kings", "note": "Avot places unavoidable life and death under a final accounting before the King, tightly joining Malik, din, and personal debt."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c4d70c73a07658e56fc7", "ref": "Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "People pass before God like a flock", "note": "The Mishnah says all humanity passes before God on the New Year like sheep, uniting the commentary's judgment day and herd imagery in a single Jewish liturgical account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-63a6e5465ea7a5362919", "ref": "Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "all who enter the world pass before God for judgment", "note": "The Mishnah makes universal judgment resemble a passing flock, closely joining the commentary's herd image to the day of reckoning."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d0fa768a529944360795", "ref": "Sifre Deuteronomy 49", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Walking God's way is imitation of God's traits", "note": "The midrash reads “walk in all his ways” as imitating God's compassion and other attributes; it turns the commentary's literal path joined to worship into an ethical practice of mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-00f079699571cb51ad6c", "ref": "Sirach 28:2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Forgive a neighbor and one's own sins are forgiven", "note": "Sirach directly joins forgiving another's wrong with forgiveness when one prays, adding a Jewish ethical interpretation to the commentary's pairing of mercy and judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2de574b36fe1dd4c774c", "ref": "Sirach 2:6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "trust, help, make your ways straight", "note": "Sirach joins reliance on God, promised help, and straightened ways in a compact form that closely mirrors the fifth and sixth ayat's prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-18b465ffd363b9eeb625", "ref": "Sirach 42:3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Keeping accounts with a partner", "note": "Sirach treats keeping accounts with a partner as a matter of honest conduct, directly meeting the commentary's debt record and witness imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c929c7fb6d1803b6ea49", "ref": "Sirach 42:4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Accuracy in scales and weights", "note": "Sirach names exact scales and weights, a concrete counterpart to the commentary's balance, upright measure, and final judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec2cdb227f1b02e15370", "ref": "Sirach 42:7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Numbered giving and receiving", "note": "Sirach instructs that stored goods and transactions be counted, joining the commentary's written debt, due date, and fear of an error in the record."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e7cd695d4e3b6ea47ca5", "ref": "Testament of Abraham 12-13, recension A", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "records, weighing, and judgment of souls", "note": "The apocalypse's judgment tableau gathers written records, scales, and verdicts, a close later-Jewish expansion of the commentary's balance-and-account scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b466b77fd1cf4d4a641d", "ref": "Tobit 4:19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bless God and ask that your ways be made straight", "note": "Tobit's instruction makes blessing the Lord and asking for straight paths one devotional practice, matching the commentary's praise-to-guidance movement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3d00a2c5b230ac121338", "ref": "WLC:Amos.8.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "The poor are crushed by merchants", "note": "Amos condemns sellers who trample the needy, giving the commentary's fraudulent-weigher scene its concrete victims."}
