{"connection_id": "BC-c34cfc4a407f5cb14bb7", "ref": "WLC:Gen.33.14", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "I will lead slowly according to the livestock's pace", "note": "Jacob's journey places a leader ahead of children and nursing flocks, supplying a specific pastoral bridge to the commentary's guide, herd, and tired traveller."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9eb2bb7e2a33cb244ab0", "ref": "WLC:Hos.11.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "taught Ephraim to walk and carried him in arms", "note": "Hosea makes God the one who teaches a child to walk and carries him, an especially close true-Rabb counterpart to Pharaoh's claimed upbringing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-634ca3f4070b89dc603e", "ref": "WLC:Isa.1.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "children raised and brought up, yet rebellious", "note": "Isaiah's parental complaint gives a biblical counterpoint to nurture received as a claim and to the servant who must choose allegiance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4356d75230c2c4e7fffe", "ref": "WLC:Isa.11.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "root of Jesse as a signal sought by nations", "note": "The raised signal draws a people toward a resting place, a secondary biblical bridge to the commentary's sign, path, and communal destination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bfc917142b30c994a98d", "ref": "WLC:Isa.2.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "YHWH's house, taught ways, walked paths", "note": "The nations go to a house so that they may learn and walk God's paths, giving the commentary's road both a community and a destination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bc362d337e2ffad3ec77", "ref": "WLC:Isa.26.7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the path of the righteous is level", "note": "The upright God makes the righteous person's path level, directly echoing the commentary's uprightness and smoothed road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dbf2b15a684bfe626022", "ref": "WLC:Isa.30.21", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A voice identifies the road to walk", "note": "The hearer is told “this is the way, walk in it” when turning aside, directly matching the commentary's traveler who asks for a guide and straight route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f1f6f66c66ad5b540c2f", "ref": "WLC:Isa.30.21", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "this is the way; walk in it; right or left", "note": "A guiding voice gives the traveller the exact formula and directional correction developed in the commentary's guide who goes before the wayfarer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e636fbf258ade5658afc", "ref": "WLC:Isa.33.22", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "YHWH our judge, lawgiver, king, and savior", "note": "Isaiah gathers judge and king in one confession; Hebrew melek is cognate with the commentary's Malik, while the verse joins ownership to deliverance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7f90dfec174bce76e48e", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The redeemed return to Zion with joy", "note": "The travelers arrive in Zion singing, with lasting joy, giving the commentary's road a communal destination in God's house."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ea1192df62cf6f0d48c5", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "waters break out in wilderness and streams in desert", "note": "The water imagery supplies the necessary environmental counterpart to Isaiah's Way of Holiness already relevant to the commentary's straight route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f1ef0a261b705dcf7c35", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A highway called the holy way", "note": "Isaiah describes a raised road for the redeemed, called the Way of Holiness, giving a communal and sacred version of the straight path requested in the Fatiha."}
{"connection_id": "BC-adf5af364e78832840d0", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Way of Holiness; walkers do not go astray", "note": "The highway is explicitly contrasted with going astray, matching the commentary's straight communal road and its lost alternative."}
{"connection_id": "BC-564ea12bb995b3da9588", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "No danger on the redeemed road", "note": "No lion or dangerous beast is found on this highway, a concrete promise of safe travel for the people whom God guides."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e208224199a1560a2576", "ref": "WLC:Isa.40.11", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The Lord gathers and leads his flock", "note": "The shepherd gathers lambs, carries them, and gently leads nursing ewes, a precise image of divine guidance shaped as care for a herd."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bc5078ad523c0ed2c427", "ref": "WLC:Isa.40.11", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shepherd gathers, carries, and gently leads the flock", "note": "The tender leader of the flock gives a strong counterpart to hadi as both guide and herd-leader."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5a1da44e80d2be9acc3c", "ref": "WLC:Isa.40.12", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "measured waters and heavens; weighed mountains in scales", "note": "Isaiah places sky, waters, and scales in one divine act, a close counterpart to the commentary's meeting of heaven and balance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3e59895b0f7cdf0a7a79", "ref": "WLC:Isa.40.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Prepare a road for YHWH in the wilderness", "note": "The voice calls for a road to be made straight in the wilderness, matching the commentary's image of a path prepared by others for the guided traveler."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bb8046177c49ba933ccd", "ref": "WLC:Isa.40.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "prepare YHWH's way; make a highway straight", "note": "Isaiah's prepared, straight desert highway gives a scriptural form to the requested sirat as a route made ready for the divine encounter."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e15db630f764be8ae3b2", "ref": "WLC:Isa.40.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The road is leveled for the coming Lord", "note": "Valleys rise and rough ground is leveled, making straightness physical and communal as in the commentary's trodden, smoothed road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f52efa703f7f902db766", "ref": "WLC:Isa.41.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "I hold your right hand; I help you", "note": "YHWH's direct promise to hold the hand and help gives concrete form to the worshipper's request for assistance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6d20a4100687290a4a4c", "ref": "WLC:Isa.42.16", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads the blind by an unknown road", "note": "YHWH promises to lead the blind on an unfamiliar path and turn darkness to light, directly joining lostness, guidance, and divine care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-065fc91b5071a6777471", "ref": "WLC:Isa.42.16", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The guide does not abandon those he leads", "note": "The same promise says God will not forsake them, contrasting the commentary's unrecognized owner with a Lord who remains responsible for the lost."}
{"connection_id": "BC-04e3b11aa60b9f3c346c", "ref": "WLC:Isa.42.16", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lead the blind by an unknown way and make crooked places straight", "note": "Isaiah's guide leads those who do not know the route and straightens its crooked parts, directly reversing the commentary's dallin."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c74570bf4998459bf053", "ref": "WLC:Isa.43.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "called by name; you are mine", "note": "Being called by name and declared God's own directly answers the commentary's contrast between recognized ownership and the masterless animal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-91bc14edb0e02484ef39", "ref": "WLC:Isa.43.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a way in wilderness and rivers in desert", "note": "Isaiah places road-making and water-making together in an otherwise impassable land, a direct counterpart to the commentary's path and water."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bac1eb20d016cf6cefa7", "ref": "WLC:Isa.43.20", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "water in wilderness to give drink to God's people", "note": "The water is expressly given for the chosen people's drinking, adding communal provision to the commentary's individual thirsty traveller."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bb43103fbacc5a7e4105", "ref": "WLC:Isa.45.23", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "every knee bows and every tongue swears to YHWH", "note": "The universal bodily confession gives a direct biblical form to worship before the sole sovereign."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b67ddbd4b1da8c2ebdb5", "ref": "WLC:Isa.49.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no hunger or thirst; guide them to springs", "note": "The promised guide supplies water and relief from need, directly meeting the commentary's travel, thirst, and leading."}
{"connection_id": "BC-db4bc724358179336481", "ref": "WLC:Isa.49.15", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic raḥīm; Hebrew reḥem and raḥam", "note": "The source commentary links raḥīm with the womb; Hebrew uses the cognate r-ḥ-m family in this verse for both a mother's womb and compassion for its child, making the image of mercy bodily and relational."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f38c469b4bbba4aef8ef", "ref": "WLC:Isa.49.15", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew rachem, womb, and compassion", "note": "Isaiah joins a nursing child, a mother's womb, and rachem; that Hebrew root is cognate with the commentary's rahim and supplies its maternal-mercy image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-90a284d3387d88f08f76", "ref": "WLC:Isa.52.12", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "YHWH goes before and is Israel's rear guard", "note": "The divine escort ahead and behind gives a precise scriptural counterpart to the commentary's traveller held from both sides."}
{"connection_id": "BC-28b9721a1ba091a5f1e5", "ref": "WLC:Isa.55.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rain waters earth and gives seed and bread", "note": "Rain's passage into growth and food supplies a precise scriptural counterpart to clouds, plants, and completed provision."}
{"connection_id": "BC-06d2ed059c7384b7d2a8", "ref": "WLC:Isa.58.11", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "continual guidance, thirst satisfied, watered garden", "note": "Isaiah binds guidance to provision in dry ground, closely meeting the commentary's route, water, need, and nurturing Lord."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d6a5765241ceaf192c50", "ref": "WLC:Isa.59.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "crooked paths; walkers do not know peace", "note": "Isaiah's crooked paths and absence of peace provide a direct Hebrew-Bible counterpart to the commentary's route that bends away from guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9386543e856f1ed10029", "ref": "WLC:Isa.62.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "build up the highway; lift a signal for peoples", "note": "Isaiah places a raised signal and a cleared communal road in the same command, matching the commentary's opening sign and constructed path."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e39f9a926ad12e58104a", "ref": "WLC:Isa.63.14", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "livestock led down to rest by YHWH's Spirit", "note": "Isaiah compares the Spirit-led people to livestock brought to rest and connects the leading with God's name, meeting herd, guide, destination, and sign."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c5ba0aa44a7839dd6238", "ref": "WLC:Isa.66.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a mother comforts her child; God comforts Jerusalem", "note": "The maternal comparison gives rahim's nurturing register a concrete biblical counterpart in divine comfort."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7c8c3c5e2f0344d75813", "ref": "WLC:Jer.10.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "do not fear the signs of heaven as the nations do", "note": "Jeremiah joins the heavenly signs to the nations' mistaken way, directly extending the commentary's distinction between sign and Lord."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fa9c266a1c895bb2b774", "ref": "WLC:Jer.31.35", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God appoints the sun, moon, and stars for their courses", "note": "The luminaries are governed creations under God's ordinance, a direct counter-narrative to calling them Rabb."}

