{"connection_id": "BC-b1a9c935383d49696113", "ref": "WLC:Jer.31.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads exiles by streams of water on a straight path", "note": "Jeremiah pictures God guiding returning Israel beside streams and on a straight road, while calling Israel God's firstborn; this joins the commentary's water, way, and belonging-to-the-Lord images."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e17af4160036af24cfa", "ref": "WLC:Jer.31.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "led by streams on a straight, non-stumbling path", "note": "Jeremiah combines a gathered people, water, divine leading, a straight path, and freedom from stumbling in one verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e94df375550829db8c9e", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "A witnessed transaction is written", "note": "Jeremiah writes and seals the deed of purchase and obtains witnesses, matching the commentary's concern with a debt or transaction made stable through proper writing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-46f33e4f197cf77c9788", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "deed written, sealed, witnessed, and weighed out", "note": "Jeremiah's purchase preserves writing, seal, witnesses, money, and duration together, closely paralleling the commentary's debt-document scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-16112518248feb939a3e", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.11", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Open and sealed copies", "note": "The purchase deed exists in both sealed and open forms, a specific legal record parallel to the commentary's account of writing and witnesses."}
{"connection_id": "BC-07a1a1d6c845444dffc5", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.12", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Witnesses see the deed", "note": "The deed is handed to Baruch in the presence of witnesses, echoing the commentary's emphasis on a witness in a recorded obligation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2a9c75633c82de7b24d8", "ref": "WLC:Jer.32.14", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Preserve the record for later proof", "note": "The deeds are stored so they may last many days, giving a concrete scriptural purpose for accurate records beyond the immediate transaction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e41c8f9118d42cc25928", "ref": "WLC:Jer.50.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost sheep led astray by their shepherds", "note": "Jeremiah's people are lost sheep whose leaders turned them from their resting place, directly meeting wrong guidance, herd, and home."}
{"connection_id": "BC-80dec324ebef61dba179", "ref": "WLC:Jer.7.23", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "obey, be my people, walk the commanded way", "note": "Jeremiah makes obedience and walking the commanded way the condition of belonging to God, clarifying the commentary's owned servant who addresses the true master."}
{"connection_id": "BC-038978a101cef5204e78", "ref": "WLC:Jer.8.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sun, moon, and stars loved, served, followed, and worshipped", "note": "Jeremiah explicitly combines astral worship with service and following, a very close counterpart to the commentary's celestial false lords and path imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6ce941ac656aa5f729a0", "ref": "WLC:Job.31.26", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sun shining and moon moving in splendor", "note": "Job names the very visual appeal of sun and moon that makes the commentary's ascending celestial signs a test of discernment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ad63e67b479e04a5a3b", "ref": "WLC:Job.31.27", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "heart secretly enticed; hand kissed in worship", "note": "The next verse identifies the move from seeing luminaries to idolatrous devotion, making explicit the error the commentary assigns to sun-worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-65fcb87d01916f12f833", "ref": "WLC:Job.31.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "let God weigh me in just balances", "note": "Job asks for divine weighing that will disclose integrity, directly pairing balance with the final moral account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4420b723ad5d5ad12de7", "ref": "WLC:Joel.3.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The dreadful day of YHWH", "note": "The sun and moon darken before the great day of YHWH, a concrete “day of God” judgment image for the commentary's days of punishment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1fdc3f686056ddef9c2d", "ref": "WLC:Joel.3.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Rescue for those who call on YHWH", "note": "The same oracle promises deliverance to those who call on YHWH, giving the day both judgment and rescue as in the commentary's paired punishment and forgiveness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d9700e606ec5803a0271", "ref": "WLC:Josh.22.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "na'budu; Hebrew la'avod; walk all his ways", "note": "Joshua joins serving YHWH with walking all his ways; Hebrew avad is cognate with the commentary's na'budu, making its service-and-road equation concrete."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b6081bf4926f29f09dd5", "ref": "WLC:Lev.1.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "offering drawn from cattle or flock", "note": "Leviticus supplies the sacrificial category of herd and flock behind the commentary's animal separated for an offering, without its full homeward scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-66856b6ef21158b906dd", "ref": "WLC:Lev.19.36", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "just balances and just weights", "note": "The Torah's command makes an unbent balance an ethical demand, supplying the legal ground for the commentary's warning about deficient measure."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b397782de1895c089e7a", "ref": "WLC:Lev.25.55", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Israelites are my servants, brought from Egypt", "note": "Leviticus opposes Egyptian bondage to belonging as God's servants; Hebrew avadim is cognate with Arabic abd and makes the true-owner contrast explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4140ca8eee115255f66a", "ref": "WLC:Mal.3.18", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "distinguish one who serves God from one who does not", "note": "Malachi makes service to God the criterion separating two destinies as judgment approaches, closely matching the commentary's willing servant and two outcomes."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ed981e22d234a5449489", "ref": "WLC:Mic.2.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the breaker and king go before the people", "note": "Micah imagines a path opened and a king going at the people's head, a strong counterpart to the commentary's guide who precedes the community."}
