{"connection_id": "BC-cea9fcb95b342671bd2c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Wanderers cannot find a way to an inhabited city", "note": "The psalm describes hungry and thirsty travelers lost in a wilderness with no city in reach, closely meeting the commentary's lost traveler and destination-home imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4ae880e45cc5de922c47", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wandered without a way to an inhabited city", "note": "The psalm begins with people lost on a desert route and unable to find a city to dwell in, closely matching the commentary's road without its final home."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ac5694d62b5a7750a9ce", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hungry, thirsty, and fainting on the way", "note": "The travellers' thirst and failing strength give a direct biblical counterpart to the weary wayfarer who asks the Rabb for help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c25df28335a161b30f33", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The lost cry to YHWH for help", "note": "The wanderers cry to God in distress and he rescues them, matching the commentary's needy traveler who asks the Lord for aid."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bb2bf7defa5eba75ec52", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads them by a straight way to a city", "note": "YHWH guides the travelers on a straight road to an inhabited city, joining the commentary's requested guidance, straight path, and arrival place in one scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2bd46466e0145879fa85", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "led by a straight way to a city to dwell in", "note": "YHWH leads the lost travellers on a straight way to habitation, combining guidance, road, and house in the commentary's exact sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-12d1e256ac65f7e9bdbd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Thanks for steadfast love after rescue", "note": "The rescued are urged to thank YHWH for his steadfast love, linking praise to the help received along the road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a9096574d364a6ab2104", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God satisfies the thirsty and hungry", "note": "God fills the hungry and satisfies the thirsty, adding provision to the lost traveler's rescue and the commentary's water imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1d788dfe08055929f883", "ref": "WLC:Ps.116.17", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Thanksgiving offering and invocation of the name", "note": "The speaker offers a sacrifice of thanksgiving and calls on YHWH's name, matching the commentary's named offering and worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6d661bbf6c0c04fc8c8a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.116.18", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The vow is paid before the people", "note": "The speaker fulfills vows in the presence of God's people, giving a public setting to the act of offering and praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fefa73f87bca7add99cd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.116.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The offering reaches the Lord's house", "note": "The vow is fulfilled in Jerusalem, in the courts of YHWH's house, directly joining sacrifice, name, worship, and the destination house."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b5204612581fcecb6268", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.105", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lamp for my feet and light for my path", "note": "The word gives a walker light exactly at the feet and on the path, sharpening the commentary's concrete imagery of movement and guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-729a23b5a3667e6aac0d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.176", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost sheep; seek your servant", "note": "The speaker is simultaneously a strayed sheep and God's servant who asks to be sought, tightly joining dallin, herd, and worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9deb13af632844ec7357", "ref": "WLC:Ps.121.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A traveler's question about help", "note": "The pilgrim looks to the hills and asks where help will come from, closely echoing the Fatiha's tired traveler's request for help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c957c291594345bff34c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.121.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Help from the creator", "note": "The answer locates help in YHWH, maker of heaven and earth, joining the commentary's help petition to its praise of the Lord of all realms."}
{"connection_id": "BC-274a542eda9d2b5bf5e7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.121.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "YHWH is shade at your right hand", "note": "The divine keeper as shade on the traveller's side gives a compact biblical counterpart to the commentary's shade and sustaining help."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e5a24fac61f2dd44bacc", "ref": "WLC:Ps.139.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hand leads and right hand holds", "note": "The psalm makes being led and physically held together, illuminating the commentary's traveller supported while he walks."}
{"connection_id": "BC-372368a2620c6994cbcf", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's good spirit leads on level ground", "note": "The psalm asks God's spirit to lead the speaker on level ground, a direct image of the upright path and guide developed in the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-02c5c7e8cdb6a67f6e2a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teach me to do your will; lead me on level ground", "note": "Prayer for obedience and for the good Spirit to lead on level ground links voluntary service, help, and an upright route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-00faad129940ac1e7377", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Show me the way I should walk", "note": "The speaker asks God to let him hear steadfast love and show the way to go, closely joining the Fatiha's request for guidance with its reliance on mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-78c119d0d66c75889069", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's kingdom is everlasting and faithful", "note": "The psalm's account of God's enduring kingdom joins praise of divine sovereignty to the commentary's master of the judgment day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0d9aafd1ad3360c3e1a5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.15", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "All creatures look to God for food", "note": "Every living thing looks to God for sustenance, matching the commentary's picture of the needy traveler and its Lord who provides."}
{"connection_id": "BC-82aefb5c855d3ce2e4b5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.16", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God opens his hand and satisfies living things", "note": "The open hand that satisfies all living things gives a specific image for completed divine favor and care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f91fb30c2d47422b7b3d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The Lord is gracious, compassionate, and slow to anger", "note": "This praise formula names the same divine qualities as the Fatiha's mercy names and places them within a hymn of praise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3fa033e81339deb52d39", "ref": "WLC:Ps.145.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The Lord's compassion extends to all he made", "note": "God's compassion reaches all his works, concretely joining mercy to the commentary's Lord of all worlds."}

