{"connection_id": "BC-ba0a9b1f2745349cb2cd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.146.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "YHWH raises those bowed down", "note": "The psalm's raising of the bent gives a direct positive counterpart to the commentary's fallen person and its upright walker."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6af3898038a0c5585ae2", "ref": "WLC:Ps.147.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "clouds, rain, and grass on the hills", "note": "The psalm explicitly has God nourish vegetation through cloud and rain, matching the commentary's nourishing Rabb."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec8d3fc4be927a04a6a2", "ref": "WLC:Ps.148.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "sun, moon, and stars praise YHWH", "note": "The celestial bodies are themselves worshippers, reversing the commentary's scene of humans worshipping them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0e7063688211c2a43c02", "ref": "WLC:Ps.19.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "heavens declare God's glory", "note": "The heavens function as proclamation of God rather than as God, giving a concise biblical form to the sign-and-signified distinction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-937703006a81cd1a9216", "ref": "WLC:Ps.20.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The fallen opponents contrast with those who rise and stand", "note": "The psalm says others collapse and fall while the worshippers rise and stand, closely matching the commentary's contrast between falling under wrath and upright walking."}
{"connection_id": "BC-97e65973a2bbc9236192", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "YHWH is shepherd and provider", "note": "The psalm calls YHWH the shepherd of the speaker and says he lacks nothing, matching the commentary's move from Lordship to the cared-for flock."}
{"connection_id": "BC-548bdaa15bb37e47d13c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.1", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "YHWH is my shepherd; I lack nothing", "note": "The shepherd relation gives the herd a known owner whose care answers the commentary's ownerless animal and needy traveller."}
{"connection_id": "BC-92cf97072f7199b36e1c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "The shepherd gives rest by water", "note": "The flock is made to lie down in green pastures and led beside waters, combining the commentary's herd, water, and traveler's rest."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b2ad27fa7426c635b41a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.2", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "green pasture and waters of rest", "note": "The shepherd's grazing place and waters give a close biblical form to the flock's going out and returning around water."}
{"connection_id": "BC-796ce34a60f19435b6ae", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "The shepherd leads on right paths", "note": "God restores the soul and leads it on right paths, directly joining the commentary's guide, herd leader, and straight way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b0bcb60cdeb7e396cfb6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "he leads me in right paths", "note": "The same shepherd restores and guides on right paths, fusing herd leadership and the straight road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9ba9c034958e97011d45", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The path crosses a threatening valley", "note": "The speaker walks through a dark valley without fear because God is with him, a concrete image of the dependent traveler who needs help along the road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1abbf1b26e915b17ad53", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A table prepared before enemies", "note": "God provides a table in the presence of enemies, a specific image of nurture and favor amid threat."}
{"connection_id": "BC-15fee2c3df649ebb51dd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The road ends in the Lord's house", "note": "The speaker expects to dwell in YHWH's house, joining the commentary's path to a destination home under the owner's care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b220897f327d25211780", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.10", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Paths marked by mercy and truth", "note": "The psalm calls all YHWH's paths steadfast love and faithfulness for covenant keepers, joining a path to divine favor rather than treating it as mere geography."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c6206b23ea95a28cb46c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Show me your paths", "note": "The psalmist asks God to make his ways known, matching the Fatiha's direct request for guidance and the commentary's road imagery."}
{"connection_id": "BC-67efa90f74c7cebcc79e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.4", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "make me know your ways; teach me your paths", "note": "This direct prayer for taught paths is a close liturgical companion to ihdina al-sirat."}
{"connection_id": "BC-602d822cb842f78121c4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Lead me in your truth", "note": "The speaker asks God to lead him and teach him, grounding the commentary's image of a traveler who needs a guide in a first-person prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3cf527a5cafee95d7194", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Remember your compassion", "note": "The psalm asks God to remember his mercy, linking the commentary's joining of mercy with the request for a way under divine care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-19408f597744b4aa1268", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.7", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Mercy despite former sin", "note": "The speaker asks that God's mercy, rather than remembered youthful sins, govern his answer; this joins guidance with mercy as in the commentary's favored and lost paths."}
{"connection_id": "BC-830965eb94123041964d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The good God teaches sinners", "note": "God's goodness and uprightness lead him to teach sinners the way, a specific meeting of mercy, moral direction, and the path requested in the Fatiha."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1c748a5fa55f3e7cae1d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The humble are taught the way", "note": "God guides the humble in justice and teaches them his way, matching the commentary's dependent traveler and a road learned from a guide."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fb7e57137758b914376a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.31.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "for your name's sake lead and guide me", "note": "The psalm joins the divine name to being led and guided, sharpening the commentary's movement from a naming sign to a requested way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-282b975253f97da62b9d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.32.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "instruct and teach the way to go", "note": "The speaker promises personal instruction and counsel about a particular way, giving a biblical analogue to the hadi who guides a traveller."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17a506e380593effb9aa", "ref": "WLC:Ps.32.9", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "horse or mule restrained by bit and bridle", "note": "The psalm's undisciplined animal needing restraint provides a direct counter-image to the commentary's tamed camel and willing servant."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9c8515b516519edc280e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.5", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "look to him, become radiant, faces not ashamed", "note": "The psalm's radiant, unashamed faces give a specific positive counterpart to the commentary's contrasting faces, though outside its final-judgment setting."}
